WEBVTT

00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:08.110
And now...

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:11.280
the OPBF Title Match...

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.110
scheduled for 12 rounds, will begin!

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.070
The challenger arrives, headed towards the blue corner.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.570
Early in his career, he seemed destined for greater things due to his uncanny skill with counters...

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:30.630
but after a loss in a tournament he vanished from the Japanese boxing scene for over a year.{tlc last just to be sure}

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.530
Now, he's back having already outgrown the national scene.

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:39.600
Ranked 1st in the OPBF,
 the resurgent genius, Miyata Ichiro!

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:42.950
Miyata-kun!

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.950
Ichiro, please win!

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:44.600
Don't get hit in the face!

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.660
Man, he's popular.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:47.560
Seriously...

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:50.600
We've got a hardcore fan here, too.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.040
MI-YA-TA-KUN!

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:51.580
MI-YA-TA-KUN!

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:52.090
MI-YA-TA-KUN!

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.110
MI-YA-TA-KUN!

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:59.470
Now the champion enters.

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.040
17 matches, 15 wins, 2 losses.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.520
Among those 15 wins, 12 were KOs, he's definitely a hard puncher.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:08.640
With devastating left and right hooks that have been compared to a crocodile's jaws,

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.130
will he be able to rip apart the challenger's aspirations!?

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:19.070
The OPBF Champion,

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.640
Arnie "Crocodile" Gregory!

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:23.550
Hey, not bad!

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.140
Man, he looks tough!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:29.430
Those Americans sure know how to show off, don't they?

00:01:29.430 --> 00:01:31.050
He's Australian.

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:31.930
What!?

00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.160
But he's white!

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.110
America isn't even in the OPBF region.

00:01:42.190 --> 00:01:43.340
Did you catch that, Ippo?

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:44.540
Yes.{tlc is this really just "YES"?}

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:47.520
That right he was throwing just to warm up was razor sharp.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.770
He's in great condition.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.540
He'll be gunning for him from the first round.

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.960
Yes, he has a certain air about him too.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.020
The aura that genuinely strong people have.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.810
He's definitely skilled,

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:01.560
and he's never been beaten by KO.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:03.680
I guess he's the real deal.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:07.640
Both fighters head to their corners.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:13.890
He's got a lot of his color back since the weigh-in,

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:18.430
but there's no way he completely recovered in one day.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.700
The cheaper the construction, the easier it falls apart.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.300
There's no need to wait for that.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.410
I'll put him down as soon as it starts.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.920
For now, keep an eye on him.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:32.410
Get a sense for how he fights and learn his timing and habits.{check}

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:35.420
Okay, Dad.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.720
The time has come...

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.960
for the OPBF Title Match!

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.470
And the bell...

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:43.970
has now...

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.220
been rung!

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:55.390
Will Japan's prized genius conquer the Pacific region as his first step toward the world stage?

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:00.230
Or will the crocodile's jaws chew apart the challenger's dream?

00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.240
The sudden death counter...

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.240
versus the destructive power that shatters bones!

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.330
This is a match to keep your eyes on!

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:09.200
Whoa!

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:13.250
The champion suddenly charges in!

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.210
The challenger is caught off guard!

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:20.460
A right!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.700
Miyata-kun's expression changed!

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.220
That just shows how dangerous that was.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:29.930
He's coming, Ichiro!

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.770
He pours it on!

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:34.720
The challenger is already trapped against the ropes!

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:35.920
He's fast too.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.240
There's no time to try and time a counter.

00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.160
He's got good rotations on his combos too.

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:42.920
If Miyata tries anything half-assed, he'll be the one who ends up getting countered.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.740
H-He's strong.{alpha timing check}

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:52.240
<i>He's got good eyesight and he's really good at dodging.</i>

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.620
<i>But how long will he be able to keep it up?</i>

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:06.300
Not giving me much of a chance to relax, are you, Champion?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:11.660
A single counter and he's gone!

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:13.380
Truly lightning speed!

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:17.520
This speed is the essence of Miyata Ichiro!

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.550
W-What did he throw?

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:20.220
I couldn't see it!

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:22.910
It was a right counter, like this.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.150
<i>Dumbass.</i>

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.530
<i>It was a short left straight.</i>

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:30.490
<i>Although, I guess it was too fast for an amateur to catch.</i>

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:32.740
The champion must be surprised as well!

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:36.540
After all, the opponent that he had been on the attack against seemed to vanish in an instant!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.780
<i>This is the first time in a fight that someone was able to just vanish from out in front of me.</i>

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:46.010
<i>I'm going to have to revise my approach here.</i>

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:49.380
<i>This challenger...</i>

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:51.510
<i>is strong.</i>

00:04:51.940 --> 00:04:53.870
That's the first time the champion has put his guard up.

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:56.810
It means he's decided to take things seriously.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:05:01.960
Since he's up against a young challenger in his first title match,

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:03.950
he probably planned on landing one splashy shot...

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.820
that'd pin him down physically and mentally.

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:10.540
However, it didn't work out like that.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.360
Miyata's not the type to choke from getting anxious.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:16.040
On top of that, Arnie was the one who ended up getting hit.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:18.740
From here on out, playtime's over.

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:20.170
The champion's gonna get serious.

00:05:21.650 --> 00:05:22.730
Serious...

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.710
Ichiro!

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:27.560
<i>I know.</i>

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:30.720
<i>Observe him for the first round, right?</i>

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.810
<i>Now then... what will you do, Arnie-san?</i>

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:37.670
A left!

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:39.570
It's clearly faster than before...

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:40.770
and sharp!

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:44.250
It lands! He's unable to dodge it!

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:46.020
<i>It's extending farther than I thought.</i>

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.030
<i>I'll have to step around it instead of swaying to avoid it!</i>

00:05:50.260 --> 00:05:52.780
The challenger is cut off!

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.580
He's caught again!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:55.480
<i>He's good...</i>

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:57.330
<i>He read my sidestep.</i>

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.030
His jaw is sent flying at the ropes!

00:06:02.030 --> 00:06:04.000
It's only a jab, but look at this power!

00:06:04.880 --> 00:06:06.830
Whoa, did it get to him?

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:11.260
<i>I thought he was supposed to just come at me with left-right hooks.</i>

00:06:11.260 --> 00:06:13.000
<i>That's the champion for you.</i>

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.720
<i>He's got his boxing down.</i>

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.450
Left, left, left!{check alpha time}

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:18.060
There's no time to return fire!

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.890
It's like he's saying, "Go ahead, throw a counter if you can."

00:06:21.890 --> 00:06:25.140
With that many fast lefts thrown so compactly...

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.480
Miyata will have his hands full with defense.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.070
Timing a punch to that is gonna be tough.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.400
Take a good look, Ippo.

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:35.550
This is another way to
 keep someone from using counters.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:38.580
He can't escape from the neutral corner!

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:40.700
The footwork that the challenger is so proud of is locked down.

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.330
Now, what can he do?

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.290
A razor sharp left grazes his face!

00:06:45.450 --> 00:06:47.370
Now what!?

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.650
<i>Dad...</i>

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:50.530
<i>that's enough observation, right?</i>

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.930
He goes in to fight it out!

00:07:01.930 --> 00:07:05.280
He challenges the powerful champion to an exchange of blows!

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:07.650
He's going to stay put and try to fight it out?

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:10.830
He's really getting nailed!

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.190
This is too reckless, Miyata!

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:13.260
No.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.200
Calm down and look closer.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.880
During that close range exchange,

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:28.460
he's watching the champion's fast left...

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.130
<i>And...</i>

00:07:30.130 --> 00:07:31.480
<i>is steadily landing counters.</i>

00:07:33.850 --> 00:07:35.410
He wins out!

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:37.470
The champion is pushed back!

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:43.980
Miyata escapes from the corner!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.480
The challenger is really putting on an amazing display!

00:07:47.870 --> 00:07:49.330
I can't believe it.

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.070
Does that mean Miyata...

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.690
...can see those fast jabs in slow motion?

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:56.410
A-Amazing...

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.290
He used the left too much.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.390
Too much?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:04.040
The scary thing about Miyata is his ability to study his opponent.

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.540
If he gets hit with a punch, the timing gets burned into his body...

00:08:08.540 --> 00:08:12.080
which means he'll be able to counter it the next time.

00:08:12.580 --> 00:08:14.610
<i>If you use the same punch twice...</i>

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:16.550
<i>it'll be returned at you with double the force.</i>

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.160
<i>Even if we punch at the same time, Miyata's punch lands first.</i>

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:22.070
<i>He's on a different level when it comes to speed.</i>

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.310
Miyata lowered his guard!

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:30.810
That's...

00:08:32.570 --> 00:08:34.190
That's the Detroit style,

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:37.820
the front-facing, offense-oriented variation.

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.450
<i>The atmosphere's...</i>

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:47.330
<i>getting tense.</i>

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:51.840
<i>There's no telling what could happen at any second.</i>

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:54.230
<i>When a counter puncher fights...</i>

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:57.180
<i>there's always a unique kind of intensity.</i>

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.580
<i>However, I've never seen another fighter...</i>

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:04.350
<i>that could silence an entire audience.</i>

00:09:18.080 --> 00:09:19.740
Both fighters move in at the same time!

00:09:21.870 --> 00:09:24.620
The champion throws his left!

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.880
He's cut down!

00:09:36.410 --> 00:09:40.830
The prince's blade, the cross counter explodes!

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:50.600
Both fighters move in at the same time!

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:53.480
The champion throws his left!

00:10:02.710 --> 00:10:05.530
He's cut down!

00:10:05.530 --> 00:10:09.750
The prince's blade, the cross counter explodes!

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:15.250
The OPBF Champion is skillfully put down!

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:16.830
Nice work, Miyata!

00:10:16.830 --> 00:10:17.960
Miyata-kun!

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:20.220
Ichiro, that was wonderful!

00:10:20.590 --> 00:10:21.590
ONE

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.490
Now the count.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:23.330
TWO

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.720
Will the champion stand up!?

00:10:23.720 --> 00:10:25.260
Arnie!

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:26.010
THREE

00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:27.220
<i>Don't get up! Let that be the end of it!</i>

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:28.680
FOUR

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.650
<i>Arnie's left managed to graze me.</i>

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:32.340
FIVE

00:10:32.210 --> 00:10:35.270
<i>I might have gotten a down, but that gave me chills.</i>

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.240
Get up, Arnie!

00:10:36.770 --> 00:10:37.770
SIX

00:10:37.240 --> 00:10:38.530
Are you going to let it all end here!?

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.280
In a place like this!?

00:10:40.280 --> 00:10:43.030
Don't get up!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.030
Just stay down!

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:44.610
SEVEN

00:10:44.780 --> 00:10:46.090
H-He stands!

00:10:46.090 --> 00:10:47.540
But he can't hide his damage!

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:49.040
Will he be able to continue!?

00:10:49.440 --> 00:10:52.040
<i>I guess he's not so soft that he would stay down after one shot.</i>

00:10:52.380 --> 00:10:55.570
<i>That's what I'd expect out of the champion.</i>

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.290
I'm up. I can go on.

00:10:58.090 --> 00:11:01.320
<i>If one shot won't keep him down, then two or three...</i>

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.300
<i>I'll hit him as many times as it takes.</i>

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:05.140
Box!

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:07.140
The match continues!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:14.010
There's the bell!

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:15.970
He wasn't able to finish it,

00:11:15.970 --> 00:11:20.730
but the challenger clearly had the advantage at the end of the first round.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:22.700
Nice work, Miyata!

00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.750
So close!

00:11:23.750 --> 00:11:25.110
Take him down next!

00:11:25.110 --> 00:11:26.820
You can take the belt!

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:29.360
Looking good, Ichiro-kun!

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:31.080
The champion really felt that one!

00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.850
Looks like things are about even.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:38.780
But, he was dominating...

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:41.090
We're at a clear disadvantage in terms of power.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:42.960
He was just holding him off with sheer speed.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:45.850
The difference in speed wasn't that big.

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:50.200
The reason I was able to counter him was because he used his left so much,

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:51.970
and I was able to study the timing.

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:55.730
That's a title holder for you.

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:57.200
Yeah.

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:58.400
He's strong,

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.240
and I don't get the feeling that he's shown all he has.

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:04.300
You should assume he recuperates well.

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:06.410
It'll be trouble if this gets drawn out.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.110
Pour it on while he's still damaged!

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:12.370
<i>I've learned the rhythm of his left.</i>

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.730
<i>I'll hit him with my right as many times as it takes.</i>

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:18.620
I didn't see that right cross coming.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:19.880
It really got me.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.280
Don't talk,

00:12:21.280 --> 00:12:23.130
just steady your breathing.

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.410
Damn it!

00:12:24.410 --> 00:12:25.630
He really nailed me.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:27.850
Don't get upset, just be calm.

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.140
I <i>am</i> calm, Mr. Sakaguchi!

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:34.460
Why do you think I put the bait out there?

00:12:35.810 --> 00:12:39.880
He was just faster than I expected, so he was able to nip me a little.

00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.150
Thanks to that, now I'm sure...

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:46.110
he'll take the bait again,

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.660
and that's when I'll finish him.

00:12:49.360 --> 00:12:52.410
Next time he draws the cross of the cross counter,

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:57.910
it'll be a cross of blood raining down on him.{tlc}

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:02.380
Bloody Cross.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.500
Round 2!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:06.750
Box!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.210
The champion's still hurting!

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:14.540
This is your chance!

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:15.440
All right!

00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:16.930
Lay into him before he gets it together!

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:18.840
The challenger goes on the attack!

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:21.150
He tears into the champion who's still reeling from his damage!

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:22.850
It's a barrage!

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:24.900
He's not waiting for a chance to counter this time!

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.920
S-So fast...

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:31.490
That's another good thing about Miyata.

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:35.670
Even though he's so good at counters, he doesn't rely solely on them.

00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:39.300
He doesn't stay on the defensive and can pour on the pressure himself.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.530
But...

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.000
I think he still has a preference.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.010
It'll be a counter that ends it.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:49.220
Counters are something that are really important to Miyata-kun.

00:13:50.530 --> 00:13:53.390
<i>I have a counter that I can finish people off with.</i>

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:56.520
<i>Even without relying on brute force,</i>

00:13:56.520 --> 00:13:58.890
<i>I can KO anyone.</i>

00:13:59.540 --> 00:14:00.620
<i>Yes...</i>

00:14:00.620 --> 00:14:02.900
<i>In the end, it'll come down to a counter.</i>

00:14:03.220 --> 00:14:05.150
The champion desperately fights back!

00:14:07.080 --> 00:14:10.240
But the lefts cut through the air fruitlessly!

00:14:10.240 --> 00:14:12.200
A-Amazing.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:14.730
It's not like the champ's attacks are weak or anything...

00:14:14.730 --> 00:14:17.270
...but he dodges them so gracefully.

00:14:17.270 --> 00:14:18.490
It's mesmerizing.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.250
<i>Nice lefts.</i>

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:22.660
<i>They're more like straights than jabs.</i>

00:14:22.660 --> 00:14:25.080
<i>I can tell how dangerous they are from the way they slice the air.</i>

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:28.980
<i>These could probably beat anyone...</i>

00:14:28.980 --> 00:14:30.340
<i>except me!</i>

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:33.260
The champion throws his left!

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:34.510
<i>Here!</i>

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.500
But a right is timed against it!

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:41.520
A masterful cross is being drawn!

00:14:42.300 --> 00:14:44.770
Bloody Cross.

00:14:50.530 --> 00:14:51.630
Whoa!

00:14:51.630 --> 00:14:53.740
The challenger's head is knocked toward the sky!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:56.280
The one who's hurt is the challenger!

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:58.320
<i>Wh-</i>

00:15:00.940 --> 00:15:02.750
<i>What just happened?</i>

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:08.100
The challenger is down!

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.550
The counter failed!

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:14.910
Impossible!

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:17.630
Miyata's counter failed?

00:15:17.630 --> 00:15:20.680
The timing was perfect!

00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.580
I was so sure it had landed.

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:24.810
So why is Miyata-kun down!?

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.220
Can the challenger stand?

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:29.030
ONE

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:32.320
Or will it be a sudden turnaround KO loss?

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:31.370
TWO

00:15:33.020 --> 00:15:34.020
THREE

00:15:33.510 --> 00:15:35.260
<i>What just happened?</i>

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:37.360
<i>Did I screw up the timing?</i>

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:39.460
<i>I thought I landed the counter.</i>

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:41.340
<i>W-Why am I the one who's down?</i>

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.330
FOUR

00:15:41.810 --> 00:15:42.840
Get up!

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:43.910
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:15:42.840 --> 00:15:44.510
It's still just the second round!

00:15:44.510 --> 00:15:45.680
Get it together!

00:15:45.680 --> 00:15:49.340
Miyata-kun, you can do it!

00:15:46.390 --> 00:15:47.920
<i>Calm down...</i>

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.350
<i>I must have messed up the hand positioning.</i>

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.510
FIVE

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:52.910
<i>It's just one of the risks of using counters.{missing line around here, check ref seems to say "fight"}</i>

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.060
<i>Focus,</i>

00:15:55.060 --> 00:15:56.850
<i>and this time without fail...</i>

00:15:56.270 --> 00:15:56.840
SIX

00:15:57.520 --> 00:15:59.330
<i>cut him down!</i>

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:00.850
He's up!

00:16:01.700 --> 00:16:02.630
Box!

00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:05.750
The champion goes in without hesitating!

00:16:05.750 --> 00:16:08.820
The challenger wants to hang back and let the damage run its course!

00:16:09.520 --> 00:16:12.540
<i>I wonder how many people in this arena...</i>

00:16:12.540 --> 00:16:16.200
<i>understand what the champion just did.</i>

00:16:16.200 --> 00:16:17.450
Go!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:19.970
You've got the counter that can put down anybody!

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:22.680
Screwing up once or twice won't matter if you can turn it around with just one punch!

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:24.170
He didn't screw it up!

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.580
If anything, his timing and speed were perfect.

00:16:28.580 --> 00:16:30.490
It wasn't a mistake!?

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:32.560
I'm sure the majority of the people here...

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.160
are certain he took that right because a mistake was made when he used the counter.

00:16:36.160 --> 00:16:38.420
Even Ichiro himself thinks so...

00:16:38.420 --> 00:16:40.600
That's how unexpected it was.

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:46.600
Why would the champion go for an exchange of lefts if he knew that he loses out in speed?

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:49.440
Counter punchers study their opponents very closely,

00:16:49.440 --> 00:16:52.110
so why would he use the same punch so many times?

00:16:52.830 --> 00:16:55.030
I should've questioned it.

00:16:55.030 --> 00:16:57.610
I should've realized sooner!

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:00.860
<i>Let's start over...</i>

00:17:00.860 --> 00:17:02.120
<i>I have to read his rhythm.</i>

00:17:02.550 --> 00:17:04.310
The challenger gets some space.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.870
Has he recovered? This is some cautious footwork.

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:08.230
A left!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.750
But it's dodged with a head-slip!

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:10.990
This is some beautiful dodging!

00:17:10.990 --> 00:17:13.640
At long range, the challenger displays a clear advantage!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.410
Keep watching it closely...

00:17:15.410 --> 00:17:17.930
Take a good look at it, Ichiro Miyata.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.010
That left is starting to look tempting, right?

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.760
Go for it.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:25.080
<i>This is it!</i>

00:17:25.080 --> 00:17:26.160
<i>No doubt about it. {jama: added (due to timing reasons i put another line here. TL/TLC forgive me D:)}</i>

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:28.520
<i>If I step in with this timing, I can definitely land it!</i>

00:17:29.140 --> 00:17:30.270
<i>Next time a left comes,</i>

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.770
<i>I'm going in!</i>

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:33.130
He's going for it!

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:34.090
Listen up!

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:36.170
Pry your eyes open and watch closely.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:39.810
Next time Miyata draws the cross for his counter,

00:17:39.810 --> 00:17:42.030
it's going to be stained red...

00:17:43.190 --> 00:17:44.580
with Miyata's blood.

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:48.580
<i>Blood...</i>

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:50.940
<i>A cross...</i>

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:52.080
<i>of blood?</i>

00:17:52.570 --> 00:17:54.590
The champion throws his left!

00:17:55.320 --> 00:17:56.260
<i>No way... {jama: added}</i>

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.090
<i>Is that...</i>

00:17:58.090 --> 00:17:59.470
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:18:01.330 --> 00:18:03.590
<i>...the Bloody Cross?{alpha time check}</i>

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.180
A clean shot from the prince.

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:09.890
<i>My timing is perfect!</i>

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:10.960
<i>Got you!</i>

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:18.440
<i>He bent his elbow...</i>

00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:21.450
<i>...to alter the angle of the punch!?</i>

00:18:21.450 --> 00:18:22.980
<i>I didn't screw up!</i>

00:18:22.980 --> 00:18:25.060
<i>He was aiming for...</i>

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:26.450
<i>my counter!</i>

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:30.950
A right turns his jaw upward!

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:32.960
A left!

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:34.460
<i>It was on purpose!?</i>

00:18:34.850 --> 00:18:36.460
Right!

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:40.490
<i>That left was to get me to throw my counter...</i>

00:18:40.490 --> 00:18:42.470
<i>to allow me to learn its timing.</i>

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.800
<i>He threw it on purpose!?</i>

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.270
A left-right combo!

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:52.350
The challenger is being hammered!

00:18:59.730 --> 00:19:01.490
It's another down!  {check for proper use of It's}

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:03.200
The challenger's second down!

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:06.420
The champion's hidden strength erupts!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.200
H-He was really wailed on...

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.200
ONE

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.710
The ring is being stained in blood!

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.210
TWO

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:15.210
Will he be able to stand?

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:15.670
THREE

00:19:15.210 --> 00:19:19.380
The momentum from when he steps in for his counter really worked against him.

00:19:19.380 --> 00:19:20.870
He's really in trouble.

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:23.710
It really is a bloody cross.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:24.860
Stop being impressed!

00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:26.490
You have to cheer for him!

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:28.220
This down is serious!

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:30.480
No, it <i>is</i> impressive.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:33.630
This is some real high level stuff that you won't see too often.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:34.730
Takamura-san...

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.130
Using your elbow to knock the cross counter upward...

00:19:38.130 --> 00:19:40.270
and then nailing the open jaw with a right.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:43.260
It might seem like a simple enough counter-killer,

00:19:44.810 --> 00:19:46.100
but...

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:51.060
being able to pull something like this off in a matter of seconds?

00:19:51.060 --> 00:19:53.450
You're a boxer, you should know how impressive that is.

00:19:54.830 --> 00:19:56.540
This champion is strong.

00:19:57.080 --> 00:20:00.460
If you want to avenge Miyata,
 be careful when you face him.

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:01.740
"Avenge?"

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.480
What's that supposed to mean?

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:05.220
What are you saying?

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.740
It's not over yet!

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.020
There's no need for me to do anything!

00:20:10.020 --> 00:20:12.350
Miyata-kun won't let it end like this!

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:15.110
Whoa!

00:20:15.110 --> 00:20:18.080
He starts to pound the mat in frustration!

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.810
An unusual sight from the usually cool challenger!

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:21.820
Ichiro... {jama: added}

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:24.180
<i>Damn it...</i>

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:27.220
<i>for him to go after my counter like this.</i>

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:29.830
<i>I've never been this pissed before.</i>

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:32.870
<i>It feels like he just ripped the pride out of my chest.</i>

00:20:34.050 --> 00:20:36.820
<i>I won't lose like this!</i>
